# Serves dist/ with clean URLs and answers unknown URLs with dist/404.html
# (status 404). The Dockerfile copies the build to /app/dist and runs Caddy
# with this file: that is how Fly.io deploys, and Railway too, since it
# builds a Dockerfile whenever it finds one.
# Without the Dockerfile, Railway's Railpack uses this file in place of its
# single-page-app default (which answers unknown URLs with the home page)
# once the service variable RAILPACK_SPA_OUTPUT_DIR=dist is set: sitelo isn't
# a framework Railpack detects. Railpack builds in /app, so the output lands
# in /app/dist there too.

:{$PORT:80} {
	root * /app/dist
	encode zstd gzip
	try_files {path} {path}/index.html
	file_server
	handle_errors {
		rewrite * /{err.status_code}.html
		file_server
	}
}
